The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (cdns->roles[cdns->role]->resume)
    cdns->roles[cdns->role]->resume(cdns, power_lost);
Reason:
This unconditionally calls the resume callback of the new role even when a role switch occurred during resume (role_changed true). In host mode, cdns_host_resume() assumes the xhci-hcd device is already probed and calls usb_hcd_is_primary_hcd(), but after start() registers the device, its probe is deferred during the resume path, leading to a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!role_changed && cdns->roles[cdns->role]->resume)
    cdns->roles[cdns->role]->resume(cdns, power_lost);
Reason:
By adding the `!role_changed` condition, the resume callback is skipped when a role switch occurred during resume. The start() operation already initializes the new role sufficiently for the resume, so calling resume() is unnecessary and unsafe. This prevents the NULL pointer dereference while allowing the xhci-hcd device to be probed after the resume sequence completes.

